#sunshine-ffmpeg (patched FFmpeg for Sunshine)

This is a companion build-time dependency for the Sunshine (game stream host)
SlackBuild.  It is NOT a general-purpose FFmpeg.

Why it exists
------------
Sunshine does not use FFmpeg's public API.  It calls FFmpeg-internal Codec
Bitstream (CBS) functions (ff_cbs_init, ff_cbs_read_packet,
ff_cbs_write_fragment_data, ff_cbs_insert_unit_content, and the private headers
libavcodec/cbs_h264.h / cbs_h265.h) to rewrite H.264/HEVC SPS bitstreams
(bitstream restrictions, NVENC SPS handling).  These symbols are not exported by
a stock FFmpeg, so Sunshine must be linked against the LizardByte patched
FFmpeg that compiles the CBS internals into a separate static libcbs.a and ships
matching static libavcodec/libswscale/libavutil/libSvtAv1Enc/libx264/libx265
libraries.

What it installs
----------------
Only static libraries and headers, under:

  /opt/sunshine-ffmpeg/ffmpeg/{include,lib}   (FFmpeg + CBS + codec libs)

These are consumed by the sunshine SlackBuild via:
  -DFFMPEG_PREPARED_BINARIES=/opt/sunshine-ffmpeg/ffmpeg

The build uses the LizardByte "build-deps" project to compile FFmpeg (plus
AMF, x264, x265, SVT-AV1, nv-codec-headers, Vulkan headers) from source.
CUDA-LLVM is disabled so the CUDA toolkit is not required; NVENC is still
available via the header-only nv-codec-headers.

Homepage: https://github.com/LizardByte/build-deps
